ure approved by a Śiva temple.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "sivamaRqaladiksa": [{"id": "SivamaRqaladIkzA", "headword": "शिवमण्डलदीक्षा", "headword_slp1": "SivamaRqaladIkzA", "fold": "sivamaRqaladiksa", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "śivamaṇḍala-dīkṣā (EI 32), same as śaiva-dīkṣā, śiva-dīkṣā.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "sivapaYcayatana": [{"id": "SivapaYcAyatana", "headword": "शिवपञ्चायतन", "headword_slp1": "SivapaYcAyatana", "fold": "sivapaYcayatana", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "Śiva-pañcāyatana (EI 27), a Śiva temple consisting of five shrines.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "sivasTala": [{"id": "SivasTala", "headword": "शिवस्थल", "headword_slp1": "SivasTala", "fold": "sivasTala", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "śiva-sthala (CII 2-1), probably, the same as dharma-sthāna, or a Śiva shrine.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "sivatiTi": [{"id": "SivatiTi", "headword": "शिवतिथि", "headword_slp1": "SivatiTi", "fold": "sivatiTi", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "Śiva-tithi (EI 5), same as Śiva-rātri or Śiva-caturdaśī.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}], "sivayogin": [{"id": "Sivayogin", "headword": "शिवयोगिन्", "headword_slp1": "Sivayogin", "fold": "sivayogin", "headword_language": "sa", "source": "indian-epigraphical-glossary", "senses": [{"gloss": "Śiva-yogin (SITI), a Śaiva ascetic.", "gloss_language": "en"}]}]}